.TH CODEXFLARE-MANAGE 1 "2026-11-01" "Codexflare 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codexflare-manage \- manage the per-user customized Codex copy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codexflare-manage
.B status | install | uninstall
.br
.B codexflare-manage launch
.RI [ application-arguments ... ]
.br
.B codexflare-manage configure
.RI { show | check | set | import-video | import-background }
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B configure
Read or update local settings with JSON output. Requires Codexflare 0.2.0 or later.
Use configure show to read settings and configure check to inspect compatibility.
Use configure set patch.json to preview a partial update; add --save to save it.
Use configure import-video FILE or configure import-background FILE to import
media without selecting it. Close the editor before writing. Saving does not
apply settings; use install separately when ready.
.TP
.B status
Report runtime compatibility and desktop-entry ownership.
.TP
.B install
Create a patched copy from saved settings and update the user menu entry.
Quit the customized Codex normally first. A running copy is never replaced.
.TP
.B launch
Start the customized copy, or fall back to the system application if the
source changed or the copy is unavailable. Forward additional arguments.
.TP
.B uninstall
Restore the previous menu entry. Keep settings, media, backups, and runtime.
No running process is stopped.
.SH REMOVING THE RPM
Run codexflare-manage uninstall before removing the codexflare package.
If the package is removed first, the retained per-user launcher falls back
to /usr/bin/chatgpt. User data is not deleted by RPM removal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR codexflare (1)
